<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Carnutes</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 51 BCE (approx.) · capital Cenabum</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Gallic people of the middle Loire, whose land held the annual assembly of the druids and whose massacre at Cenabum began the revolt of 52 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Carnutes lived between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seine">Seine</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/loire">Loire</a>, around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chartres">Autricum</a> (Chartres) and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orleans">Cenabum</a> (Orléans). Caesar reports that their territory was considered the centre of all <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>, where the druids met each year in a sacred place to judge disputes.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They were ruled by a nobility, and Caesar installed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tasgetius">Tasgetius</a> as their king, but he was murdered in 54 BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orleans">Cenabum</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/loire">Loire</a>, was a busy trading town where Roman merchants lived.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In early 52 BCE the Carnutes killed the Roman traders at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orleans">Cenabum</a>, the signal for the revolt of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vercingetorix">Vercingetorix</a>. Caesar sacked the town and in 51 BCE executed their leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gutuater">Gutuater</a>. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chartres">Autricum</a> became Chartres and Cenabum was refounded as Aurelianum, later Orléans.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/carnutes.jpg" alt="Carnutes" width="320" height="325"><figcaption>Image: User:Feitscherg · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_Gallia_Tribes_Towns.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 51 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> – <a href="